        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>A new full-commercial treadmill from a gym brand typically costs about $9,000 to
            $14,000 before delivery and tax, while a remanufactured ex-gym machine from the same brands
            usually costs about $2,500 to $4,000.</strong> The figures below are listed dealer and maker
            prices, checked November 2026; quotes for a gym buying several machines can come in lower.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>New club treadmills:</strong> <a href="/star-trac-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Star Trac</a>'s 8 Series TR at $9,199 new, True's TC900
            at $10,099 to $13,399 depending on console, a Life Fitness Integrity+ for facilities at $11,247
            and the Woodway 4Front at $13,995 (all checked November 2026).</li>
            <li><strong>Commercial machines sold to homes:</strong> Life Fitness's own consumer store
            listed new "outlet" Integrity treadmills at $5,940 and $7,183, depending on console (checked
            November 2026). Its home models are priced console by console in our <a href="/how-much-does-a-life-fitness-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Life Fitness treadmill cost</a> guide.</li>
            <li><strong>Remanufactured belt treadmills:</strong> a <a href="/precor-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Precor TRM</a> 835 from $2,495 and a Matrix
            T3x at $3,799 at US resellers (checked November 2026). Slat-belt machines cost more: a
            remanufactured Woodway 4Front was $9,599.</li>
            <li><strong>On top of the price:</strong> room-of-choice installation ran $449 to $699 at one
            large reseller, and extended service plans from about $299 to $1,749 depending on length and
            whether the use is home or commercial.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If you are pricing a treadmill for a home and have not yet decided that it needs to be a
            commercial one, start with our broader guide to <a href="/how-much-does-a-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">how much a treadmill costs</a>,
            which covers every tier from walking pads up. This page stays at the top end of that range.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="prices-by-brand" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Commercial Treadmill Prices by Brand</h2>
<p>
